There are certain traits that if you can easily get redundant you
should.  Some quest artifacts act as luckstones but the character
should carry a blessed one anyways.  Some quest artifacts grant
reflection or magic resistance but the character should have them
by other means anyways.  The priest's quest artifact doesn't do
any of those, so it's still worth duplicating whereever possible.
And the priests quest artifact is worth having in its own right.

Since a priest can't #twoweapon (IIRC), it's possible to get
reflection from: SDSM, silver shield, amulet.  Pick any two ;^).
The possible sources of MR are GDSM and CoMR.  Pick any two ;^).
Combine them and you get an arguably ideal mix of "oR, GDSM,
[oR, [oMR, b luckstone and a spare in the bag.  It's arguable
because a priest can do equally well with a robe and no shield.
Spells versus defense, Nethack always has options that are both
correct.  But redundant in 3 major issues is not a bad idea.

